<title>HONG KONG: Harbour Centre 1996 net up 24.8 percent.</title>
<headline>Harbour Centre 1996 net up 24.8 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   116.0     vs 93.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    41.0	vs 38.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  24.2 gain vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    364.6     vs 292.1</p>
<p>    Turnover		     1,142.3   vs 1,432.3</p>
<p>    Company name		 Harbour Centre Development Ltd</p>
<p>    Books closed		 May 21-27</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   June 2</p>
<p>NOTE - Harbour Centre is a hotel and property investment firm.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain on disposal of hotels and investment property in the United States on February 29, 1996.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 52 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of 11 cents) vs 48 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
